<!-- THE NAME OF THIS FILE HAS TO SORT AFTER scene.rml. Not a preference:
     the CLI scans *.rml alphabetically and compiles them "as one document",
     and on the WEB runtime a markup file sorted before the one holding the
     ScriptedLayout kills every Luau script in the build — `ScriptAsset
     doesn't have a generator function table`, background fill drawn and
     nothing else. It only bites with a WGSL shader in the file, so the CLI
     viewer never shows it and neither does --verify. This was `cards.rml`
     and that is exactly why the web build was dead. rive.yaml has no
     ordering key, so the filename is the only lever; tools/rml-order-test.mjs
     guards it. -->
<Rive version="1" kind="fragment">
    <!-- =========================================================================
         CARDS — one artboard per rank, built from shared components.

           Corner   the rank glyph and the suit under it. Top-left only.
           Plate    the face. Last child, so it draws underneath. Its Face's
                    opacity is the Card view model's `plate`: 1 on a card, 0
                    on the ink-only instance a tank card draws into the ink
                    atlas (table.luau), so the rank prints OVER the creatures.
                    It is DEEP WATER, not cream, and it carries no edge of its
                    own: every card's face is a window onto a tank, so all the
                    plate ever is is what shows through the seam around that
                    window, and in cream that seam read as a hard white line
                    drawn round every card. The card's edge is the RIM
                    (crt.wgsl), a shaded bevel with a material on it.
           Card A … Card K
                    the layouts: ONE corner and the plate. There is no turned
                    bottom-right copy — a card here is never read upside down,
                    and the second corner only crowded the tank. NOTHING ELSE is
                    drawn on a face — no pips. The number IS the tank: a 7
                    holds seven bodies (tanks.csv), an ace one apex predator,
                    the court one creature from the roster, a species per suit.
           [FPO] Pip
                    generated suit marks (a fish, a bubble, a shell drawn from
                    primitives; the starfish is real art). Placed on no card.
                    Ethan's rule: a generated symbol never ships and is always
                    flagged FPO — keep the tag on it, and put it on nothing.

         table.luau instances Card <rank> per card with that card's view model
         (rank text, ink colour, which suit is 1). Hierarchy order: FIRST child
         draws on TOP. Ids here are 2:*; scene.rml owns 0:*, tuner.rml 1:*.
         ========================================================================= -->
